  "title": "The Dandelion Launch Network",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A block gardener wants to scatter square fantasy seeds across an empty grid, but one launcher keeps dropping them in a pile. Landing seeds depress miniature release platforms for preloaded launchers farther away, spreading a bounded zigzag trail until the final seed raises a miniature garden sign.",
  "hook": "The first seed has to start the next journey.",
  "visible_action": "Seed cubes arc between soft platforms; platforms dip; preloaded cartoon arms release in sequence; a zigzag planting pattern fills the grid.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A chain can distribute outputs instead of piling them at its start.",
  "gate": "Fantasy block seeds and preloaded low-force toy launchers; show finite stored energy, not perpetual motion. No ecology, germination, or weapon-building claims.",
